# Line endings, stated once.
#
# This repository is consumed by Linux and by sh/lua, and the pre-commit hook requires LF in the *stored*
# blob. Without this file the worktree on Windows is CRLF over an LF index, and that mismatch is a trap for
# every editing tool: an `edit` anchor silently misses because it matches bytes, and the hook refuses a
# legitimate change because `git add` stores the carriage returns it found on disk. It cost a run of fixes
# on the whatsapp branch their diff topics, and two commits were refused before anyone worked out why.
#
# `eol=lf` states the intent, so the hook goes back to being a backstop instead of a minefield.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts are the exception, and only for the worktree: the stored blob stays LF, which is what the
# hook checks, while cmd.exe and PowerShell get the endings they expect on disk.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries are never converted. `text=auto` detects most of them; these are named because a wrong guess
# would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
*.wasm binary
